ead the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Do-support is not added to a can question.","B":"Can does not take an -s ending.","C":"Be is not added before can.","D":"**Can** moves before she; no do is added."}}},{"id":"a8f785a8-0696-5c12-a711-abe1a611df7f","topicSlug":"modals-ability","level":"A2","prompt":"Use managed to for one successful event: “Yesterday, we managed to ____ the travel leaflet despite the difficulty.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"translated"},{"id":"B","text":"translate"},{"id":"C","text":"translates"},{"id":"D","text":"translating"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"After **managed to**, the next verb returns to its base form.","explanation":"**Managed to translate** describes successful completion on that occasion.","keywords":["past-achievement"],"skill":"past-achievement","contextKey":"modals-ability-4","fingerprint":"2a1575c7fc8f90a63c566a88d7a02388cafd61f12f75b534366edb6084baaa90","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-ability"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["After **managed to**, the next verb returns to its base form.","**Managed to translate** describes successful completion on that occasion.","Choose **translate**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The past marking is on managed, not on the infinitive.","B":"**Managed to translate** describes successful completion on that occasion.","C":"The infinitive after to has no -s ending.","D":"Managed in this meaning takes a to-infinitive, not to + -ing."}}},{"id":"cd631123-bbf3-5a86-a260-633de3ee276b","topicSlug":"modals-ability","level":"A2","prompt":"Express future ability with able: “Next month, they will ____ the travel leaflet without help.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"are able to translate"},{"id":"B","text":"be able translate"},{"id":